# Test: `ze config validate` refuses two operator SPD entries whose order the
# configuration leaves undecided, and accepts the entries a total order separates.
# Spec: spec-rfc4301-architecture-gaps (AC-15, RFC 4301
#       Section 4.4.1: the management interface "MUST support (total) ordering of
#       these entries, as seen via this interface.").
#
# QUESTION: does an operator who writes two overlapping `vpn ipsec policy` entries
# and leaves both at the default order (1000) learn it at commit, from the command
# they type, with both names and the command that separates them? A unit test
# proves verifySPDOrder (engine/rfc4301_spd_order_total_test.go); only this test
# proves the refusal reaches the operator through the YANG parse, the ike plugin's
# offline verifier (validateIPsecSections -> verifySPDOrder) and the CLI's print of
# the operator error.
#
# VALIDATES:
#   seq=1 `wide` (10.0.0.0/8 -> 192.0.2.0/24) and `narrow` (10.1.0.0/16 ->
#         192.0.2.0/25), both directions, every protocol, both left at the default
#         order: a packet from 10.1.0.1 to 192.0.2.1 matches both, so validate exits
#         1 naming both entries and the shared order 1000, with the fix
#         `set vpn ipsec policy wide order 1001`;
#   seq=2 the same two entries with `narrow` at order 900: accepted, the order
#         decides;
#   seq=3 two entries at the default order whose local prefixes are disjoint
#         (10.1.0.0/16, 10.2.0.0/16): accepted, no packet matches both, so no order
#         between them is observable;
#   seq=4 two entries with one selector in one direction (`out` outbound, `both`
#         both directions, same prefixes) at distinct orders: refused whatever the
#         orders, because the dataplane holds one entry per selector, with the fix
#         `delete vpn ipsec policy out`.
# PREVENTS: the D-2 defect, where each entry was judged alone, so two overlapping
#   entries at the default order committed and the kernel decided between them by
#   the sequence it received them in.
#
# Every cmd asserts its own exit with exit=. Needles carry no ':'.
#
# RED PROOF: in internal/component/ike/engine/config.go validateIPsecSections,
#   delete the `verifySPDOrder(cfg)` step: seq=1 and seq=4 exit 0, red. In
#   engine/spd_order.go spdOrderRefusals, delete the `if a.Order != b.Order {
#   continue }` guard: seq=2 is refused, red. Make spdPoliciesOverlap answer true:
#   seq=3 is refused, red.
#
# `unmatched bypass` is written in every block so the implicit-discard refusal
# (refuseImplicitDiscard) stays out of the subject.

stdin=tie:terminator=EOF_TIE
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy wide {
			action bypass
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 10.0.0.0/8
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/24
			}
		}
		policy narrow {
			action discard
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 10.1.0.0/16
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/25
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_TIE

stdin=ordered:terminator=EOF_ORDERED
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy wide {
			action bypass
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 10.0.0.0/8
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/24
			}
		}
		policy narrow {
			action discard
			order 900
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 10.1.0.0/16
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/25
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_ORDERED

stdin=disjoint:terminator=EOF_DISJOINT
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy first {
			action bypass
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 10.1.0.0/16
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/24
			}
		}
		policy second {
			action discard
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 10.2.0.0/16
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_DISJOINT

stdin=same:terminator=EOF_SAME
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy out {
			action discard
			order 1000
			direction out
			local {
				prefix 10.1.0.0/16
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/24
			}
		}
		policy both {
			action bypass
			order 1500
			direction both
			local {
				prefix 10.1.0.0/16
			}
			remote {
				prefix 192.0.2.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_SAME

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=tie:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=vpn ipsec policy narrow and vpn ipsec policy wide overlap in selector and direction and share order 1000
expect=stdout:contains=set vpn ipsec policy wide order 1001

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=ordered:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=disjoint:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=same:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=vpn ipsec policy both and vpn ipsec policy out name the same selector in the same direction
expect=stdout:contains=delete vpn ipsec policy out
